💡 **SUGGESTION: no negative test that a benign includeIf survives the Guard 1b strip**

The strip is deliberately value-scoped (`--unset-all "$include_key" '.*git-credentials-[^/]*\.config$'`), but the new test only asserts the credentials-pointing entries and file are **gone**. A regression that drops the value regex and unset-alls the *entire* key (or removes unrelated `includeIf.gitdir:` entries — e.g. a developer-configured include on a self-hosted persistent workspace) would pass every current test while breaking unrelated behavior.

One fixture line + one expect closes it:

```dart
// in buildFixture (checkoutV7 branch):
git(['config', 'includeIf.gitdir:$work/.git/benign.path', '${root.path}/not-credentials.config']);

// in the v7creds test:
final benign = Process.runSync(realGit, ['config', '--local', '--get-all',
    'includeIf.gitdir:$work/.git/benign.path'], workingDirectory: m.work);
expect((benign.stdout as String).trim(), isNotEmpty,
    reason: 'the strip must be value-scoped — benign includes survive');
```

